The Japanese word for crisis, Ke-Ke, is made up of two words: danger and opportunity. 

@fundstrat’s Tom Lee said yesterday in his Macro Minute that investors tend to focus on the “danger” in a crisis and then later chase the “opportunity.” He outlined why they should avoid that strategy this time around, even though tech stocks have been dropping sharply.

